   "body": "**Revue adversariale (Opus 5.5) : CHANGEMENTS DEMANDÉS** — tête af44e76e381eb5d16957f2bd57f3bdb40c313368\n\n1. **Moyenne** — PR body `Closes #286`; `docs/lots/LOT-168-forum-list-completeness.md` §Pending capture. Only categories 1, 2 and 10 are checked (`R285a`-`c`). #286 asks that every category show its REST count and that every injected forum be checked. Seven entries stay unchecked: `Photonumerique/Divers-7`, `Win-9x-me`, `Concours-2`, `Ressources`, `Divers-5`, `AchatsVentes/Divers-4`, `Regles-coutumes`. No capture issue tracks them: I searched for `subcategories`, and only #285 (closed) comes up. **Fix:** open the `host: mac` capture issue and change to `Refs #286`, saying what is left.\n2. **Basse** — `ForumListCompletion.swift:14-28`. A page link that has no REST row is always kept. Scenario: one of those seven injected entries is gone from HFR, or its title is spelled differently in REST. The user then sees a dead forum, or the same forum twice (slug path plus `subcat` path). I measured this: with the old table put back, Programmation gives 28 entries instead of 27 (the extra one is « PDA »). This exceeds the REST count, which the spec says should not happen. **Fix:** treat an injected entry with no REST match as stale and drop it, or list this limit in the spec.\n3. **Détail** — `ForumListCompletion.swift:6` still says \"Programmation 14 of 27\"; the page now gives 13. The comment at `ForumListParserTests.swift:174` still says \"6 of those 14\".\n4. **Détail** — `ForumListCompletionTests.swift:101`: the test title says \"none is of a category not captured yet\", but the test asserts nothing about that.\n5. **Détail** — When REST and the page disagree on order (C# before C++ in REST), « Delphi/Pascal » and « Flash/ActionScript » end up between « C++ » and « C#/.NET managed ». This follows the stated rule but reads oddly. Note it in the spec.\n\n**Vérifié**\n- `swift test --filter 'ForumListCompletionTests|ForumListParserTests|RESTBrowsing'`: 32 tests pass.\n- `swiftlint lint --strict` on the touched files: clean.\n- Read the titles in `R285a`-`c` myself: « PDA » and « Biblio Links » are absent; the 16 remaining injections (Hardware 1, Overclocking 1, Programmation 14) are all present; `&amp;` is decoded by `RESTDocument`.\n- Probe: with the old table put back, 3 tests fail (count 28 ≠ 27).\n- Simulated the Programmation merge order by hand.\n- `category >= 1` (`RESTBrowsingClient.swift:90`) is not covered by any test.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
