   "body": "**Revue adversariale (Opus 5.5) : CHANGEMENTS DEMANDÉS** — tête 9415594 (round 2)\n\nRound 1 follow-up:\n- (1) Fixed. The PR body says `Refs #286` and lists what is left. #929 is open with `### Summary`, one label per axis, `host: mac`, and the same origin as #286.\n- (2) Fixed. The spec has a \"Limits\" paragraph saying a page link with no REST row is kept, so a list can end up longer than the REST count.\n- (3) **Partly fixed**: see finding 1.\n- (4) Fixed. The title of `injectionsAgainstCapture` now matches what the test checks.\n- (5) Fixed. The spec's \"Limits\" paragraph describes the order difference (C# before C++ in REST).\n\nFindings:\n1. **Basse** (stale doc): two places still say \"Programmation 14 of 27\". With PDA and Biblio Links removed from the table, the page now gives 13.\n   - `Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRClient/REST/RESTBrowsingClient.swift:51`: doc comment of `subcategories(in:)`.\n   - `docs/lots/LOT-021-forum-list-parser.md:88`: rewritten by the PR but kept \"14 of 27\".\n   - Fix: write \"13 of 27 with the injection table\" in both places. HFR-PROTOCOL.md:300 is fine as written.\n\n**Vérifié**\n- `swift test --filter \"ForumListCompletionTests|ForumListParserTests|RESTBrowsing\"`: 32 tests in 3 suites pass.\n- `swiftlint lint --quiet` on the touched folders: no warnings.\n- Grepped `14 of 27|reaches 14` in Packages and docs.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
